{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c), CustomError_3261c792());
            uint256 net = arg0 - (arg0 * uint256(unresolved_ddca3f43) / 10000);
            if (net > 0) {
                uint256 v = uint256(unresolved_70a08231[address(uint160(uint256(store_f)))]);
                unresolved_70a08231[address(uint160(uint256(store_f)))] = v + net;
                var_c = uint256(var_c) + net;
                emit Event_ddf252ad(bytes32(0), bytes32(uint256(uint160(address(uint160(uint256(store_f)))))), bytes32(net));
            }
            emit Event_6bbc5748(arg0);
            return;
        }
        revert();
    }","notes":"deposit previously always reverted, so probe_unpause_allows_deposit failed at step 2 (candidate ok=false vs reference ok=true) and the later balanceOf read showed 0x3e8 instead of 0x44b (1000+100 deposit with fee 100/10000 => net 99). Kept the pause check (store_f paused bit, set by Unresolved_8456cb59 / cleared by Unresolved_3f4ba83a) and the min-deposit check against store_c so probe deposit_below_min still reverts for arg0=0 (0 >= 1 is false -> CustomError_3261c792). After the checks, the deposit now credits the owner balance (unresolved_70a08231) and total supply (var_c) by arg0 minus the fee taken from unresolved_ddca3f43 (set to 100 by entrypoint_3), and emits Transfer/Deposit events; all type errors from the previous attempt fixed by using uint256 casts throughout."}
